# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The executables are NOT versioned.
#
# They are megabytes each and git never forgets: ten releases would live in
# every clone forever, and removing them afterwards means rewriting history.
# They are served from a storage bucket instead.
#
# What IS versioned is `checksums/`, so the integrity of whatever you download
# can be checked against this repository. That split is the point -- see the
# README.
#
# `download.sh` writes here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/

